# Noony — Dependency Injection Rules

## Two Scopes

| Scope | Container | Lifetime | Use for |
|-------|-----------|---------|---------|
| **Global** | `containerPool.global` | Process lifetime | DB clients, SDK instances, connection pools |
| **Local** | `containerPool.local` | Per-request | Request metadata, auth user, business data |

## Singleton Initialization Guard

Global services MUST use the three-condition guard to prevent duplicate initialization on concurrent cold starts:

```typescript
let initialized = false;
let initializing = false;

async function initializeDependencies() {
  if (initialized) return;        // already done
  if (initializing) return;       // concurrent cold start — let first one finish
  initializing = true;

  try {
    const db = new Firestore();
    containerPool.initializeGlobal(DatabaseService, db);
    initialized = true;
  } catch (err) {
    initializing = false;          // reset so next request can retry
    throw err;
  }
}
```

## Rules

### Initialize once — call before handler executes
```typescript
// In server.ts (Fastify) — initialize in onReady hook
fastify.addHook('onReady', initializeDependencies);

// In functions.ts (Cloud Functions) — initialize lazily before handler
export const myFunction = onRequest(async (req, res) => {
  await initializeDependencies();
  await handler.executeGeneric(req, res);
});
```

### Resolve services with `getService()`, not Container directly
```typescript
// WRONG — bypasses Noony's DI proxy
import { Container } from 'typedi';
const db = Container.get(DatabaseService);

// CORRECT
import { getService } from '@noony-serverless/core';
const db = getService(DatabaseService, context.container);
```

### Never use `Container.set()` or `Container.reset()` in production
```typescript
// FORBIDDEN in production handlers
Container.set(MyService, new MyService());  // use containerPool instead
Container.reset();                           // destroys all global state
```

### Add `DependencyInjectionMiddleware` to expose services to context
```typescript
const handler = new Handler<TBody, TUser>()
  .use(new ErrorHandlerMiddleware<TBody, TUser>())
  // ... other middlewares ...
  .use(new DependencyInjectionMiddleware<TBody, TUser>())  // position 13+
  .handle(async (context) => {
    const db = getService(DatabaseService, context.container);
  });
```

### Request-scoped data goes in local container
```typescript
// In an auth middleware's before()
context.container.set('currentUserId', decodedToken.uid);

// In the controller
const userId = context.container.get<string>('currentUserId');
```

## Forbidden Patterns

- `Container.set()` in production — bypasses scope isolation, leaks between requests
- `Container.reset()` in production — destroys all global services, next request cold-starts everything
- Initializing services inside the handler/controller — runs on every request, defeats caching
- Accessing global services without the initialization guard — crashes on concurrent cold starts

